            <title id="f3t">Elevation, drawn to scale at ten units per centimeter: the rover’s front face on the left with three time-of-flight sensors stacked on it, and three dashed sight lines running right — the bottom beam to a 3 centimeter cube, the middle beam over it to a 6 centimeter cube, the top beam over both to a hatched obstacle at the far right.</title>
